  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7dae8d5d-2970-59ed-b461-3707b05f1264" activityNameId="c2d9d83e-1383-5d47-93f0-f286114e3253" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Disposal, residue from TiO2 prod. SO4, 30% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Disposal, residue from TiO2 prod. SO4, 30% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% residue from TiO2 production (sulfate process); . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O 296000; O 319600; H n.a.; C n.a.; S 28600; N n.a.; P n.a.; B 7.1933; Cl n.a.; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag 0.714; As 0.62521; Ba 149.04; Cd 11.748; Co 1.3453; Cr n.a.; Cu n.a.; Hg n.a.; Mn n.a.; Mo n.a.; Ni n.a.; Pb n.a.; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn n.a.; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti 140000; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 128100; Fe 18400; Ca 21400; Al 17700; K n.a.; Mg 30000; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 60.4%. Additional solidification with 0.4 kg of cement.;; UUID: 0060e86b-ecd1-49ff-8c8b-3c7b352d90c6
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. Expenditures for solidificalion with cement (user-specified option)
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Minimal long-term emissions are the emissions until the carbonate buffer in the landfill is used up. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr).
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0060e86b-ecd1-49ff-8c8b-3c7b352d90c6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
